{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/trouble-tickets/1554657-editing-posts-and-the-spam-filter","id":1554657,"title":"Editing posts and the spam filter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Trouble Tickets"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-24T21:16:52-07:00","id":1554657,"title":"Editing posts and the spam filter","content":"Is it possible to remove the way editing a post can cause the post to get caught by the spam filter? Of course the spam filter is necessary to keep someone from making dozens of posts, but does the spam filter need to pick up someone editing an existing post? It's kind of frustrating when I make a post, notice that I forgot a word or made an egregious spelling error and then when I go back to edit the post, it gets locked because the system thinks it's spam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-09T06:02:59-07:00","id":1558748,"title":"","content":"It would be great if, instead of catching the post or edit in the spam filter and waiting for a moderator to approve it, the poster could instead be informed that the post or edit will end up needing review if he proceeds, and does he want to do that? <br /> <br /> I just edited a post of mine where the only thing I changed was to replace &quot;Ami&quot; with &quot;am I&quot;. That got it tagged as spam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></